 ## Google Drive
 
-Drive features are opt-in. Saved routes sync in their own app-data file. When
-**Sync settings too** is enabled, an allowlisted settings snapshot syncs in a
-separate file with tombstones, conflict handling, monotonic timestamps, and a
-local baseline snapshot. API keys, panel geometry, the working route, and any
-setting that controls where data is sent (such as the AIS filing destination)
-remain device-local.
+Drive is opt-in: nothing goes to Drive until you press **Sync with Google Drive** in
+**Saved routes**. On every Sync:
+
+| What | Box unticked | **Use settings from Drive on this device** ticked |
+|---|---|---|
+| Saved routes (and saved GPS tracks) | synced both ways | synced both ways |
+| Your aircraft and its figures, default speed, climb rate, the flight plan form's pilot details, your frequency and chart-placement corrections | synced both ways | synced both ways |
+| Display settings: layers, overlays, colours, sizes, opacities, page setup, language, AI provider and model | **backed up** only; this device's own are kept | synced both ways |
+| API keys, the AIS filing address, window positions, theme, the working route, per-device switches (voice, follow, lock, brightness, sharing, offline maps) | never leave the device | never leave the device |
+
+- Routes are in `navaid-routes.json`. Settings sync both ways in `navaid-settings.json`, with
+  tombstones, conflict handling, monotonic timestamps and a local baseline snapshot. Unticked,
+  a device leaves the other devices' display settings in that file untouched.
+- **Backup:** every Sync also writes all of this device's settings to
+  `navaid-settings-backup.json`, ticked or not. **Restore settings from Drive** brings them back
+  on this device, once, and reloads. A device that has never backed up is asked first
+  (*Restore it on this device?*, then *Replace the backup?*), so a new phone's first Sync
+  never overwrites the real backup unasked.
+- The note under the box says it plainly: the backup includes your pilot details (name,
+  licence, phone, email) and aircraft.
 
 Clearing browser storage removes local state but does not implicitly delete
 Drive app-data. The route library UI owns its Drive actions.
